 ## Notes
 
+- **Accounting boundary.** All linked accounts are in scope. Posted purchases
+  count as spending; confirmed movements between linked accounts do not count
+  again. Pending activity remains visible in Transactions but is excluded from
+  posted analytics. Refunds marked confirmed/likely reduce spending, on the
+  refund posting date. Person-to-person reimbursement matching is not automated.
+- **Review candidates after upgrading.** Existing unconfirmed transfer guesses
+  now remain in totals. Totals can increase until genuine transfers are confirmed;
+  this prevents an incorrect guess from silently hiding spending.
+- **Deduplication.** Reimporting the same provider transaction ID updates its
+  existing record. Distinct IDs are not deleted just because amounts and dates
+  match: these may be real repeated charges. Independently linking the same bank
+  account twice under different provider identities is not automatically merged.
+- **Supported scope.** This pass hardens existing ingestion and accounting; it
+  does not add a Venmo connector, currency conversion, suspicious-charge engine,
+  or investment analysis. Payment-service records follow the same accounting
+  rules when available through the existing data source. Use one reporting
+  currency; aggregate charts do not convert or separate currencies.
+
 - **Single-threaded SQLite.** Concurrent API requests are serialized at the DB level. Fine for single-user.
 - **No migration framework.** Column additions and backfills are applied idempotently on startup by `app/db/schema_patches.py`; only larger structural changes may warrant a manual rebuild. Back up `~/.vibeledger/vibeledger.db` before changes.
 - **Link token expiry.** Plaid link tokens expire after 4 hours. The 20-minute session TTL mitigates this in practice.
