@@ -2,6 +2,37 @@
 
 This roadmap tracks the long-running Candor-inspired work. The repository is the durable source of truth; chat is for decisions and coordination.
 
+## Current focus: trustworthy existing accounting (2026-09-02)
+
+Feature expansion is paused. First make the existing income, spending, recurring,
+and transaction-review views trustworthy as more checking, credit-card, and
+payment-service accounts are linked. Investment analysis is out of scope.
+
+Agreed accounting contract:
+
+- All linked accounts are inside the reporting boundary. Confirmed movements
+  between them are internal transfers; an external movement remains income or
+  spending. Credit-card purchases count at posting, and confirmed repayments do
+  not count again.
+- Pending activity is visible for inspection but excluded from posted analytics.
+- An unconfirmed transfer candidate remains counted until confirmed. Do not
+  silently remove genuine spending based only on equal amounts and nearby dates.
+- Repeated ingestion of the same provider transaction is idempotent. Distinct
+  purchases with the same merchant, date, and amount must remain distinct.
+- Historical totals recompute as imported history and reconciliation change.
+- Use simple, durable categories and shared deterministic accounting functions;
+  optional agents should query bounded API results rather than ingest the ledger.
+- The main visual answers how spending compares with the comparable prior period.
+  Account freshness is supporting context, not a new landing screen.
+- Automatic person-to-person reimbursement matching, forecasting, and the broader
+  optimization suite remain deferred.
+
+The hardening pass covers API/SQL-view consistency, sync corrections and removals,
+transfer review state, chart/drill-down parity, and focused synthetic regression
+tests. CI enforces at least 80% combined statement/branch coverage over `app/`;
+frontend tests, typechecking and builds are separate checks. This percentage does
+not claim coverage of all React or Streamlit UI code.
+
 ## Status vocabulary
 
 - `idea`: captured, not yet committed
